WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.030
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:28.300 --> 00:29.760
Nakarai.

3
00:33.410 --> 00:35.020
What's that?

4
00:35.710 --> 00:37.110
A penguin.

5
00:37.110 --> 00:39.300
As a thank-you for the watermelon.

6
00:50.440 --> 00:52.080
Is this how you get in?

7
00:52.080 --> 00:54.560
Yeah, a bit further that way.

8
01:01.810 --> 01:04.000
Whoa.

9
01:04.000 --> 01:05.970
Don't just watch.

10
01:05.970 --> 01:08.560
You're making me do everything.

11
01:09.180 --> 01:11.880
It doesn't match my personality.

12
01:11.880 --> 01:14.180
Same here, you know?

13
01:15.040 --> 01:16.938
All right.

14
01:17.830 --> 01:19.720
I'm doing double syrup.

15
01:19.720 --> 01:21.800
Whoa!

16
01:21.800 --> 01:25.400
Oh, crap! Can you get me some tissues?

17
01:25.400 --> 01:26.503
It's empty.

18
01:26.503 --> 01:29.170
Sorry, there's more in my bedroom closet.

19
01:29.170 --> 01:30.290
Okay.

20
01:30.290 --> 01:32.580
This is bad...

21
01:34.090 --> 01:36.370
Man, this...

22
01:36.970 --> 01:40.270
It's going to smell like strawberry...

23
01:58.440 --> 01:59.960
Yum!

24
02:00.650 --> 02:03.150
I might have invented something.

25
02:03.150 --> 02:05.130
Double syrup is the best.

26
02:07.740 --> 02:09.470
Did you know?

27
02:09.470 --> 02:13.250
Apparently all shaved ice syrups taste the same.

28
02:13.250 --> 02:16.270
Huh? Really?

29
02:16.270 --> 02:18.880
Strawberry, lemon, blue Hawaii...

30
02:18.880 --> 02:21.310
They're all the same sweetener.

31
02:28.580 --> 02:31.440
But it's strawberry and lemon...

32
02:31.440 --> 02:35.510
Apparently the scent and color create the illusion of taste.

33
02:35.510 --> 02:38.690
In the end, people prioritize what they see.

34
02:40.110 --> 02:42.420
I kind of feel tricked.

35
02:46.830 --> 02:50.310
By the way, why a double?

36
02:50.310 --> 02:53.150
What? The syrup?

37
02:53.150 --> 02:54.710
The bed.

38
02:58.080 --> 02:59.490
Is that bad?

39
03:00.490 --> 03:04.400
No, but it was a little surprising.

40
03:04.990 --> 03:10.610
You must've been pretty confident, expecting us to get together like that.

41
03:13.860 --> 03:16.580
It was like making a wish.

42
03:16.580 --> 03:18.630
And it came true right away.

43
03:21.500 --> 03:22.980
A wish?

44
03:24.310 --> 03:27.470
A wish for you to come here.

45
03:33.141 --> 03:35.141
Oh, sorry.

46
03:39.680 --> 03:43.235
[Shoko Hagiwara]

47
03:44.700 --> 03:46.370
Gonna answer?

48
03:46.370 --> 03:48.900
It's fine. I'll call back later.

49
03:48.900 --> 03:52.850
Answer it. It might be urgent.

50
03:56.640 --> 03:58.320
Hello?

51
04:03.670 --> 04:07.560
Hey, you're not coming home for Obon?

52
04:08.430 --> 04:10.760
I'm busy with this and that.

53
04:10.760 --> 04:13.980
Busy? When you don't even have a girlfriend?

54
04:15.550 --> 04:17.570
It's work.

55
04:17.570 --> 04:20.820
I was looking forward to seeing Kaori...

56
04:22.590 --> 04:25.440
Stop bringing that up.

57
04:25.440 --> 04:29.320
Give marriage and the future some more thought, okay?

58
04:29.320 --> 04:32.410
I'm busy now. I'll contact you later.

59
04:32.410 --> 04:33.850
Wait!

60
05:01.500 --> 05:03.470
What are you looking at?

61
05:03.470 --> 05:05.750
I hear a festival.

62
05:05.750 --> 05:07.170
A festival?

63
05:16.330 --> 05:17.810
You're right.

64
06:17.900 --> 06:19.938
I'm hungry.

65
06:20.794 --> 06:22.299
Let's eat here.

66
06:22.299 --> 06:23.592
Nice.

67
06:26.094 --> 06:30.350
So, I, Adachi, am getting married.

68
06:30.350 --> 06:32.880
- Huh? - Huh? With who?

69
06:32.880 --> 06:34.730
With who?

70
06:34.730 --> 06:37.980
Obviously, the person I'm currently dating.

71
06:37.980 --> 06:42.460
Well, it feels like you prefer girls you met three days ago.

72
06:42.460 --> 06:45.010
Stop. You make me sound crazy.

73
06:45.010 --> 06:46.590
No, I kind of get it.

74
06:46.590 --> 06:49.580
I didn't expect you to get married for a while.

75
06:49.580 --> 06:53.200
Well, that was the plan, but...

76
06:54.400 --> 06:56.650
Could it be...

77
06:56.650 --> 07:00.390
We're having a baby.

78
07:00.390 --> 07:02.980
- Seriously? - Wow, congratulations!

79
07:02.980 --> 07:04.490
That's amazing.

80
07:04.490 --> 07:07.177
Dang, I'm shocked.

81
07:07.177 --> 07:09.620
It's Nakarai. Nakarai!

82
07:09.620 --> 07:12.340
Hurry! Faster, faster!

83
07:12.340 --> 07:14.340
Get over here!

84
07:17.042 --> 07:19.024
Your order is here.

85
07:22.090 --> 07:24.510
Lunch? Let's eat together.

86
07:24.510 --> 07:26.160
No, I'm just getting coffee.

87
07:26.160 --> 07:28.930
Come on, just drink it here with us.

88
07:32.510 --> 07:35.720
Adachi's getting married.

89
07:35.720 --> 07:37.625
- Oh, congrats. - Thanks.

90
07:37.625 --> 07:39.260
So he's done being a playboy then?

91
07:39.260 --> 07:43.030
Come on, not you too! Just who do you think I am?

92
07:43.030 --> 07:45.810
Still, you're getting married so fast...

93
07:45.810 --> 07:48.710
Did you hear? Our co-worker Moriya's marrying too.

94
07:48.710 --> 07:51.370
Hagiwara's planning the after-party again.

95
07:51.370 --> 07:53.060
Yeah, that's right.

96
07:53.060 --> 07:54.960
Excuse me.

97
07:59.229 --> 08:01.099
I ordered too much.

98
08:03.170 --> 08:04.840
Hagiwara!

99
08:04.840 --> 08:07.320
Hey, you're eating lunch here?

100
08:07.320 --> 08:09.810
Shigeta! What a coincidence.

101
08:09.810 --> 08:12.880
I'm the one who taught you to slack off here.

102
08:12.880 --> 08:14.760
Did you?

103
08:14.760 --> 08:17.990
Hey, you broke up with your girlfriend, right?

104
08:19.310 --> 08:22.420
Want me to introduce you to someone next?

105
08:22.420 --> 08:24.070
No thanks, I don't need that.

106
08:24.070 --> 08:27.080
Hey, don't be shy.

107
08:34.830 --> 08:40.140
Hello, this is Shigeta. Yes, thank you for the call.

108
08:40.140 --> 08:42.820
Yes, thank you very much.

109
08:42.820 --> 08:46.090
Right, yes...

110
08:48.290 --> 08:50.460
That was lucky.

111
08:53.360 --> 08:54.990
I'm heading back.

112
08:54.990 --> 08:56.200
Okay.

113
09:30.160 --> 09:36.320
[Summer Festival]

114
09:36.320 --> 09:37.718
[Request for Funding]

115
09:37.718 --> 09:40.706
[Seeking individuals and companies to support and sponsor the festival.]

116
09:40.706 --> 09:41.996
[Call or visit to apply.]

117
10:17.500 --> 10:19.607
Welcome.

118
10:19.607 --> 10:21.470
Please come in.

119
10:32.420 --> 10:34.100
I'll have today's wine.

120
10:34.100 --> 10:35.260
Sure.

121
10:35.260 --> 10:36.310
Me too then.

122
10:36.310 --> 10:37.970
Okay.

123
10:37.970 --> 10:39.940
I haven't had dinner.

124
10:39.940 --> 10:43.560
I'll have the salmon pâté and whatever you recommend.

125
10:43.560 --> 10:46.070
Yes, coming right up.

126
10:54.650 --> 10:56.800
Do you come here often?

127
10:56.800 --> 10:58.680
Sometimes.

128
10:58.680 --> 11:02.350
They're open late, so it's convenient if I work overtime.

129
11:02.350 --> 11:03.970
I see...

130
11:10.690 --> 11:12.230
What?

131
11:12.890 --> 11:14.360
Are you still mad?

132
11:14.360 --> 11:15.800
About what?

133
11:15.800 --> 11:18.590
About Shigeta at lunch today.

134
11:21.730 --> 11:24.270
He has some strong quirks,

135
11:24.270 --> 11:27.680
but he's a really good senior to me.

136
11:27.680 --> 11:30.790
Mentors can mean a lot, you know?

137
11:30.790 --> 11:33.080
Don't you have one too?

138
11:33.900 --> 11:37.340
Mine was a female senior, so not especially.

139
11:37.340 --> 11:40.120
And that's not my vibe anyway.

140
11:41.080 --> 11:44.820
It's not like I chose a male senior because I wanted to.

141
11:50.170 --> 11:52.180
True.

142
11:52.180 --> 11:53.690
That's how it usually is.

143
11:53.690 --> 11:55.980
Wait, why are you saying it like that?

144
11:55.980 --> 11:57.800
Like what?

145
12:01.150 --> 12:02.960
Here you go.

146
12:02.960 --> 12:04.340
Thanks.

147
12:09.170 --> 12:12.280
This is the first time you've brought a friend, Nakarai.

148
12:12.280 --> 12:13.940
Is he from work?

149
12:13.940 --> 12:15.720
Yes.

150
12:15.720 --> 12:19.570
You never come on weekends, Nakarai.

151
12:19.570 --> 12:21.070
Because it looks crowded.

152
12:21.070 --> 12:23.000
No, not at all.

153
12:23.000 --> 12:24.780
Please come visit.

154
12:24.780 --> 12:26.020
I'll drop by sometime.

155
12:26.020 --> 12:27.350
Okay.

156
12:29.850 --> 12:32.520
Your friend is handsome.

157
12:32.520 --> 12:34.890
Does he have a girlfriend?

158
12:34.890 --> 12:36.250
Someone I'm dating?

159
12:36.250 --> 12:37.540
Yes.

160
12:40.580 --> 12:42.310
Well, of course I do.

161
12:43.360 --> 12:46.930
Wow, I'm jealous.

162
12:48.540 --> 12:52.070
I'm desperate for a boyfriend right now.

163
12:54.670 --> 12:56.970
Introduce me to someone.

164
12:58.090 --> 12:59.790
I'm rooting for you.

165
13:00.390 --> 13:05.230
Ayuko, tell them to bake the baguette a little crispier than usual.

166
13:06.870 --> 13:11.140
Okay. Manager, bread extra crispy.

167
13:31.820 --> 13:34.350
You shouldn't be like that.

168
13:34.350 --> 13:35.420
What?

169
13:35.420 --> 13:38.940
That girl is clearly interested in you, Nakarai.

170
13:38.940 --> 13:41.560
Why would you bring me there?

171
13:41.560 --> 13:42.860
You noticed?

172
13:42.860 --> 13:44.710
Of course I noticed.

173
13:45.780 --> 13:48.750
It's not like there's any real harm.

174
13:48.750 --> 13:53.080
Just so you know, I haven't done anything to make her misunderstand.

175
13:53.080 --> 13:55.200
You used her name.

176
13:55.200 --> 13:57.470
Didn't you look at the menu?

177
13:57.470 --> 14:01.220
It says "Ayuko's homemade dessert of the day".

178
14:01.220 --> 14:04.160
So asking her last name would be rude.

179
14:10.800 --> 14:13.920
I wonder why we're so upset.

180
14:15.310 --> 14:20.090
Well... in my case, it's jealousy.

181
14:27.550 --> 14:28.750
Here.

182
14:29.580 --> 14:31.410
What is it?

183
14:31.410 --> 14:35.220
Your lips are dry, even though it's summer.

184
14:35.220 --> 14:36.680
Ah...

185
14:38.080 --> 14:41.600
Put it on. Put it on for me, Nakarai.

186
14:44.050 --> 14:45.870
If you say so.

187
14:52.010 --> 14:53.770
Don't move.

188
14:59.190 --> 15:02.040
There's such a strong honey feel.

189
15:02.040 --> 15:05.820
I got it today. A souvenir from Taiwan.

190
15:07.090 --> 15:09.820
It might attract ants.

191
15:09.820 --> 15:12.290
I'll get to you before the ants.

192
15:14.020 --> 15:15.594
You know, Nakarai...

193
15:17.020 --> 15:20.240
You're surprisingly good at this. Does it come naturally?

194
15:21.170 --> 15:23.870
It's because you're so cute.

195
15:24.970 --> 15:26.660
You're annoying.

196
15:56.200 --> 15:59.370
Oh, man. I want to go home soon.

197
15:59.370 --> 16:02.180
I wish we could just teleport there.

198
16:03.710 --> 16:06.520
You're so cute when you're like this.

199
16:41.960 --> 16:45.200
Don't look. It's embarrassing.

200
16:46.430 --> 16:49.610
Treat me today, okay?

201
16:49.610 --> 16:51.090
Huh?

202
16:51.090 --> 16:52.890
Treat me.

203
16:52.890 --> 16:56.050
Sure, but... what exactly?

204
17:18.850 --> 17:22.790
Treat you here? Why?

205
17:22.790 --> 17:25.336
Because I paid for you without asking.

206
17:25.336 --> 17:27.080
Paid for what?

207
17:27.080 --> 17:29.260
Funding for the festival.

208
17:30.860 --> 17:33.000
Sorry, what do you mean?

209
17:43.330 --> 17:48.060
The other day, I saw a flyer for this festival in the shopping arcade.

210
17:48.060 --> 17:49.840
I like this kind of thing.

211
17:49.840 --> 17:51.620
Oh, is that so?

212
17:51.620 --> 17:57.020
Small festivals and rituals that would never bring in tourists.

213
18:01.650 --> 18:03.770
- Here you go. - Thanks.

214
18:07.190 --> 18:11.790
It feels like all sorts of things are being preserved here.

215
18:14.720 --> 18:16.010
Yeah.

216
18:18.180 --> 18:20.140
So I donated money.

217
18:20.140 --> 18:24.400
5,000 yen each, in your name and mine.

218
18:24.400 --> 18:26.160
Oh?

219
18:35.197 --> 18:36.617
It fell off.

220
18:40.030 --> 18:41.720
Whoa.

221
18:41.720 --> 18:44.050
- For you. - Thanks.

222
18:46.660 --> 18:48.370
Yum!

223
18:48.370 --> 18:50.020
The coffee's great.

224
18:50.020 --> 18:52.010
Let's make this with Mr. Penguin.

225
18:52.010 --> 18:54.110
We'll need condensed milk.

226
19:00.265 --> 19:02.525
Hey, do you see that?

227
19:03.700 --> 19:05.510
I know right?

228
19:05.510 --> 19:08.370
- That cotton candy looks good. - Yeah, it does.

229
19:08.370 --> 19:09.733
- Want some? - Yeah.

230
19:09.733 --> 19:11.113
Let's go.

231
19:31.590 --> 19:34.665
What happens to these after they float down?

232
19:34.665 --> 19:36.458
[Place messages and offerings to the deceased and your ancestors]

233
19:36.458 --> 19:38.250
[to drift down the river with your feelings]

234
19:39.560 --> 19:42.850
They probably collect them somewhere, right?

235
19:42.850 --> 19:46.230
It'd probably be bad if they just go out to sea.

236
19:46.230 --> 19:48.908
It'd be illegal dumping.

237
19:48.908 --> 19:51.508
Sounds weird when you say it though.

238
19:53.560 --> 19:58.450
So in the end, they can't go anywhere.

239
20:05.770 --> 20:07.230
Want to go see?

240
20:09.240 --> 20:10.550
It's fine.

241
20:34.600 --> 20:37.230
Oh, this is...

242
20:37.230 --> 20:38.740
There it is.

243
20:40.030 --> 20:41.198
You're right.

244
20:41.198 --> 20:43.110
[Sei Nakarai] [Kazuaki Hagiwara]

245
20:43.110 --> 20:46.290
Hagiwara, notice anything?

246
20:46.290 --> 20:47.750
Yeah, there it is.

247
20:47.750 --> 20:49.670
Not that.

248
20:50.460 --> 20:52.440
Huh?

249
20:52.440 --> 20:55.800
I'm talking about why our names are there.

250
20:55.800 --> 20:58.630
Because you paid for both of us?

251
20:58.630 --> 21:00.719
No, look closely.

252
21:00.719 --> 21:02.620
It's in alphabetic order.

253
21:03.209 --> 21:05.284
Aida... Ao...

254
21:07.626 --> 21:13.177
[Hirose... Hirata... Nakarai... Hagiwara]

255
21:13.860 --> 21:15.930
You're right.

256
21:15.930 --> 21:19.080
Huh? Then why are we right next to each other?

257
21:19.080 --> 21:22.680
Because I submitted my name as "Han'i". (*Nakarai can be pronounced as Han'i)

258
21:22.680 --> 21:26.250
That's why I'm right next to Hagiwara.

259
21:26.250 --> 21:29.250
I checked online. It's a real name.

260
21:29.250 --> 21:30.420
Why?

261
21:30.420 --> 21:34.270
Why? I just wanted to see us lined up together.

262
21:37.270 --> 21:42.110
Good thing there weren't any Hanyus or Hamadas.

263
21:53.030 --> 21:55.510
Let's go to the sea next time.

264
21:55.510 --> 21:58.070
Next year and the year after too.

265
21:58.960 --> 22:00.630
Why every year?

266
22:01.550 --> 22:02.940
No reason.

267
22:26.430 --> 22:28.125
What's your wish?

268
22:30.766 --> 22:32.186
It's a secret.

269
22:32.936 --> 22:34.586
I see.

270
22:36.330 --> 22:37.730
Hagiwara.

271
22:38.750 --> 22:42.830
It's a shrine, so you bow twice, clap twice, and bow once.

272
22:42.830 --> 22:45.300
I know that much.

273
22:45.300 --> 22:46.540
I thought you didn't know.

274
22:46.540 --> 22:48.550
I know.

275
23:00.640 --> 23:04.100
What does the after-party organizer for a wedding actually do?

276
23:04.100 --> 23:06.570
They said they'll let us take care of everything.

277
23:06.570 --> 23:08.042
"Us"?

278
23:11.560 --> 23:13.240
Look at my phone anytime.

279
23:13.240 --> 23:15.390
- I'm not gonna worry. - Come on, worry a little.

280
23:15.390 --> 23:18.070
Jeez, it's fine. Why do you want me to distrust you?

281
23:18.070 --> 23:19.380
Sorry.

282
23:19.380 --> 23:21.050
I can't come over tonight anymore.

283
23:21.050 --> 23:22.550
Are you alone today?

284
23:22.550 --> 23:24.780
Don't you have something to say?

285
23:24.780 --> 23:27.170
I have something to say to you.

286
23:27.170 --> 23:28.190
You do?

287
23:28.190 --> 23:31.177
It started with an email.

288
23:31.177 --> 23:32.990
That's exactly why...

289
23:32.990 --> 23:36.040
Because I don't want to regret falling for him.

290
23:36.040 --> 23:39.150
Even after I fell for you, I kept my guard up.

291
23:39.150 --> 23:42.130
And yet, every little thing you said and did had me up and down.

292
23:42.130 --> 23:45.120
We never had that kind of thing, right?

293
23:45.120 --> 23:49.620
So, after I fell in love, I fell in love again.

294
23:49.620 --> 23:51.020
You're finally back.

295
23:51.020 --> 23:52.220
Why are you laughing?

296
23:52.220 --> 23:54.030
They're leaning on each other.

297
23:54.030 --> 23:55.900
Yeah, they're well-made.

298
23:55.900 --> 23:57.410
Cheers.

299
23:57.410 --> 23:58.740
Cheers.
